      },
      "text": "Puerto Ayora"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:contentBlock_text:23638bb3309714a6",
      "field": "contentBlock.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "a19de0a40ff5e1f85ce2e839030c4cb67e35f9bea75cbef575605691f895247d",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-1794263606047-afmpnw",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "Breakfast at the hotel.\n\nTransfer to the airport for your flight to the Galápagos Islands.\n\nOn arrival at Baltra Airport, your guide will meet you, help with your luggage and show you to the bus. The drive to the Itabaca Channel, which separates Baltra from Santa Cruz, takes 10 minutes.\n\nCross the channel to Santa Cruz by motorboat in about 5 minutes. From there, we'll drive across the island by private vehicle to your hotel in Puerto Ayora, a journey of about 45 minutes. Along the way, look for the change in scenery from the rocky red terrain in the north to the lush highlands and south."
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:contentBlock_text:c7db10db06e48b32",
      "field": "contentBlock.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "b1ffa98195ae11e537263cdb6baa637d87513d9214e59e6f206e0cc9ff028480",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-1794263606047-afmpnw",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "Transfer to your hotel. After a welcome reception, check into your room and take some time to rest.\n\nYou’ll then have free time to explore the port town of Puerto Ayora, with its souvenir shops, restaurants and scenic waterfront."
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:media_alt:6a3a2631fd578dc4",
      "field": "media.alt",
      "sourceTextSha256": "713eea7e3834200d01610388104f120377d064981ecbae94f04203291ee3d7cf",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-1794263606047-afmpnw",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "A wooden boat and motorboats in the turquoise waters of Puerto Ayora harbour, Ecuador"
    },
    {
